Luna-Ruling-Collider: Lares (Tasked Spirit). A read-only collision, read-only seat.
THE DESIGN UNDER COLLISION: `git -C /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt show 9bfa4c127:bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift.mem` (the B1 lift: the browser vessel leaves the page's main thread for its own worker; the clean ceremony document, operator-APPROVED 2026-11-05, takes the secret and sends its bytes down a service-worker-brokered port to the vessel worker; each tab carries its own live session with its own unlock and one face; one vessel worker per house; typed port payloads; the vessel reads its own durability; every slice lands before the rite).
Operator rulings 2026-11-05: "Browser + Node is part of founding"; "Land all before the rite, no 'build a now, b later'"; "Multiple tabs will carry live sessions, and later can change face (one face per session)"; "realm" stays reserved for the DreamNet (a JavaScript execution context reads as a thread); the ceremony document approved.
TASK: read each carrier below (canon at the span: `/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/...`) for every design statement about the page, the browser, workers, the surface, unlock/ceremony, passphrase/passkey/PRF, keystore, seeds/keys, custody, sealing, sessions, tabs. COLLIDE each against the B1 design. Report each collision: carrier:line, the quoted statement, the B1 slot it meets, and the kind: CONTRADICTS (one must change; say which side the newer rulings favor) / EXTENDS (the carrier adds a constraint B1 must carry; name it) / STALE (the carrier describes a shape B1 dissolves; it needs truing when B1 lands) / AGREES (one line, only for load-bearing agreement). Also name any carrier statement that B1 forgot (a law, a refusal, a residual) that a slice must keep. Ignore lore and grammar that touch none of these.
OUTPUT (final message, under 900 words): grouped by carrier, CONTRADICTS first, then EXTENDS, then STALE; a closing list of the 3-6 changes B1's carrier most needs.
CARRIERS (paths under /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/ unless named): stable-founding-road.mem #/rulings ONLY (navigate by ahu slots; ~lines 126-355) and #/decisions; pono/controller-handoff.mem #/state; pono/seat-harness.mem (the ward, S2/S2b/S3 design); pono/kahua-memory-stage.mem; ../../../lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection.mem; pono/blob-carriage.mem.

